/-!
# Native four-torus cohomology coordinates and fixed generators

Actual singular cohomology is expressed through its proved canonical
evaluation pairing on the original positive-loop and ordered-minor
homology classes.  The actual pullback by the cusp matrix has the
transpose action.  Its integral fixed classes have exactly the forms
`(a,b,0,0)`, `(a,b,c,d,-b,0)`, and `(a,b,0,0)` in degrees one, two, and
three, respectively.

The generator descriptions are identities of native cohomology classes
in their actual evaluation-dual bases.  They do not redefine cohomology
as a formal dual, identify pullback with forward inverse-dual transport,
or assert an unproved cup-product comparison.
-/
